remuda: cluster join: expected the invitation line printed by `remuda cluster invite`: remuda cluster join 'remuda-join-v1 …' (quotes optional; add --yes when stdin is not a terminal)
Join using the invitation line from `remuda cluster invite`; quotes are optional. Example: remuda cluster join 'remuda-join-v1 …'

Usage: remuda cluster join [FINGERPRINT] 'JOIN_LINE' [--yes] [--bind IP[:PORT]]

Arguments:
  [FINGERPRINT]  Optional pinned fingerprint (the line already carries it)
  [JOIN_LINE]    Invitation line; quotes are optional

Options:
  -h, --help              Print help
      --bind <IP[:PORT]>  Address; omitted port defaults to 7441
      --yes               Join without the confirmation prompt (needed when stdin is not a terminal)

Next: remuda cluster join [FINGERPRINT] 'JOIN_LINE' [--yes] [--bind IP[:PORT]]
